From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:28:24 +0800
Subject: Portal dialogs: a mobile dialog wraps within the screen width

On a phone the dialog was as wide as its implicit width and ran off the screen; it now takes at most
the available width less the margins.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-27
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain bug; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: no scenario opens a portal dialog)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/42
---
 src/PortalDialog.qml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/PortalDialog.qml b/src/PortalDialog.qml
index 996b585..d30fc30 100644
--- a/src/PortalDialog.qml
+++ b/src/PortalDialog.qml
@@ -183,6 +183,8 @@ Kirigami.AbstractApplicationWindow {
             anchors.fill: Kirigami.Settings.isMobile ? undefined : parent
             anchors.centerIn: Kirigami.Settings.isMobile ? parent : undefined
             anchors.margins: Kirigami.Settings.isMobile ? glow.cornerRadius : 0
+            // A mobile dialog must wrap within the available screen width.
+            width: Kirigami.Settings.isMobile ? Math.min(implicitWidth, Math.max(1, parent.width - 2 * Kirigami.Units.largeSpacing)) : parent.width
             topPadding: 0
             bottomPadding: 0
             rightPadding: 0
